            <div xml:id="d777">

                <pb facs="0820" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-13T17:00:00+08:00">April 13, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 13—7:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>324. Mukden’s April 12, 1 p.m. to the Department and the Legation. Legation today
                    received similar report from American Consul at Dairen who added: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Although Siuyen is not in the Kwantung leased territory, I have notified
                            the Kwantung Government and police and informally requested such
                            assistance as they may be in a position to render.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Legation has informed Tokyo and Japanese Legation here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
